<title>USA: Viking Office adopts rights plan.</title>
<headline>Viking Office adopts rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Viking Office Products Inc said its board adopted a shareholder rights plan intended to protect its stockholders in the event of a proposed takeover.</p>
<p>The company said the plan guards against partial tender offers, open market accumulations and other takeover tactics.</p>
<p>Viking said the rights issued under the plan would take effect if a person or a group acquired 15 percent or more of its common stock or announced a tender offer for a 15 percent stake.</p>
<p>It said the plan was not adopted in response to any specific effort to acquire control of the company.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
